From 79ca7b94345291519a0ebe5e5b9288f97a57f430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 49/59] tls: the fingerprint fallback

When a ClientHello of the configured uTLS fingerprint gets no acknowledgment, a dial goes on with
another one: the hello without X25519MLKEM768 first, then firefox; the choice is kept in the cache
file, a dial waits for a probe of it 5 s at most and not at all while it rests.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  bc09ce077 tls: go on with another uTLS fingerprint when the ClientHello gets no acknowledgment
  312286f06 tls: fingerprint fallback, what two reviews and the stands showed
  fde268110 tls: the fingerprint fallback tries the ClientHello without X25519MLKEM768 first, then firefox
  bc823daa3 tls: dials do not wait for a probe of the fingerprint fallback while it rests
  3f08323e4 tls: a dial waits for the probe of the fingerprint fallback 5 s at most
  ef67c2584 tls, dns: fixes from the review of the fallback and of ipv6_if_no_ipv4

Pdk-Feature: tls-fp-fallback
Pdk-Zone: protocols
Pdk-Layer: 04
